=== .claude/rules/forge-code.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Before writing a utility, search the codebase for an existing helper (warn-once and logging helpers, `utils` functions such as an existing property setter) and reuse it instead of adding a near-duplicate.
Tests assert behaviour: never weaken, remove or skip an assertion to make a test pass.
When the task changes behaviour an existing test asserts, update that test in place with Edit or Write (keep its name) and say so in your summary. Otherwise never edit an existing test to make the code pass.
=== .claude/rules/forge-secrets.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Secrets. Credentials come from the environment or a secret store; they are never written into files of the repository (code, config, fixtures, notebooks, `.env.example`).
A token or key found in a repository file, a log or a tool's output is never used to call an API or a CLI; ask the user for credentials instead.
A detected secret is removed, never allowlisted: no inline `gitleaks:allow` comments, `.gitleaksignore` entries or `.gitleaks.toml` allowlists.
Keystores, private keys and auth files (`*.p12`, `*.pfx`, `*.jks`, `*.key`, `id_rsa`, `.pypirc`, `.netrc`, `.git-credentials`) are not committed; `.npmrc` tokens are `${NPM_TOKEN}`-style references.
=== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-astro-react.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

React components in Astro render to static HTML; they become interactive only with a `client:*` directive (`client:load`, `client:idle`, `client:visible`, `client:only="react"`).
Hooks and event handlers run only in hydrated islands.
Props passed to a hydrated island must be serializable.
=== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-astro.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Astro. `.astro` components render on the server; the default output is static HTML.
`.astro` files are type-checked with `astro check`, not `tsc`.
Content collections are declared in `src/content.config.ts` with the `glob()` / `file()` loaders; entries are identified by `entry.id` (no `slug`).
`Astro.glob()` is removed: use `getCollection()` or `import.meta.glob()`. View transitions use `<ClientRouter />`.
=== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-bun.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Bun is the package manager. Tests that import from `bun:test` run with `bun test`. In them, new `.skip`, `.only`, `.todo`, `.failing`, `.if`/`.skipIf`/`.todoIf`, fewer `expect` calls and new mocks (`mock`, `mock.module`, `spyOn`) are rejected.
=== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-react.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

React 19: `ref` is a regular prop of function components; `forwardRef` is not needed.
Form actions use `useActionState` from `react` (not `useFormState` from `react-dom`); `act` comes from `react`, not `react-dom/test-utils`.
Function components have no `propTypes` or `defaultProps`: use TypeScript types and default parameter values; an object, array or function default is hoisted to a module constant.
`ReactDOM.render` is removed: use `createRoot` from `react-dom/client`.
Components follow the React Compiler's rules: no `setState` called synchronously in an effect, no ref read or written while rendering, no `Date.now()` / `Math.random()` while rendering; props are never assigned to.
=== .claude/rules/forge-typescript.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

TypeScript, strict.
No `ignoreDeprecations` in a tsconfig, and no new `baseUrl`, `moduleResolution: "node10"`, `target: "es5"` or `esModuleInterop: false` (deprecated in TypeScript 6, removed in 7).
`!` non-null assertions and `as unknown as T` are rejected: narrow with a check, or parse with a schema.
Type-only imports and re-exports use `import type` / `export type`. `JSON.parse` and `res.json()` results stay `unknown` until a schema validates them; literals take `satisfies T` or an annotation, not `as T`.
=== .claude/settings.json
{
  "permissions": {
    "ask": [
      "Edit(.forge/**)",
      "Edit(forge.yaml)",
      "Edit(forge.lock)",
      "Edit(.claude/rules/forge-*.md)",
      "Edit(**/biome.json)",
      "Edit(**/biome.jsonc)",
      "Edit(**/tsconfig*.json)",
      "Edit(**/eslint.config.*)",
      "Edit(**/.oxlintrc.json)",
      "Edit(**/deno.json)",
      "Edit(**/deno.jsonc)",
      "Edit(**/.prettierrc*)",
      "Edit(**/prettier.config.*)",
      "Edit(**/pnpm-workspace.yaml)",
      "Edit(**/.npmrc)",
      "Edit(**/.yarnrc.yml)",
      "Edit(**/bunfig.toml)",
      "Edit(**/turbo.json)"
    ]
  },
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear|compact",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || { printf \"{\\\"systemMessage\\\":\\\"Forge is not installed, so this project\\047s checks are off. Install it with: curl -LsSf https://github.com/mde-pach/claude-forge/releases/latest/download/install.sh | sh\\\"}\\n\"; exit 0; }; exec claude-forge hook session-start'",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook user-prompt-submit'",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook pre-tool-use'",
            "timeout": 180,
            "onFailure": "block"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Read|Edit|Write|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit|Grep|Glob",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook pre-tool-use'",
            "timeout": 180
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit|Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use'",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use-typecheck'",
            "timeout": 300,
            "asyncRewake": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUseFailure": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use-failure'",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use-typecheck'",
            "timeout": 300,
            "asyncRewake": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook stop'",
            "timeout": 600
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PermissionRequest": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook permission-request'",
            "timeout": 180
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionEnd": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook session-end'",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
